        </fields>
      </register>
      <register>
        <name>ECCCS</name>
        <displayName>ECCCS</displayName>
        <description>ECC control and status register</description>
        <addressOffset>0x34</addressOffset>
        <size>0x20</size>
        <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
        <fields>
            <field>
              <name>ECCADDR</name>
              <description>The offset address of double word where an ECC error is detected.</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>16</bitWidth>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ECCCORIE</name>
              <description>One bit error correct interrupt enable.</description>
              <bitOffset>15</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ECCDETIE</name>
              <description>Two bits errors detect interrupt enable.</description>
              <bitOffset>14</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SYSECCBK</name>
              <description>This bit in read only to indicate whether the system memory ECC error occurs in the first 3k or later 3k region of the information block.</description>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-only</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>DF_ECC</name>
              <description>If an ECC bit error is detected in data flash, this bit will be set. And the ECCADDR records the offset address of main Flash. ECCDET bit and ECCCOR bit indicate there is a one bit error or a two bits error. This bit is cleared by writing 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>6</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OB_ECC</name>
              <description>If an ECC bit error is detected in reading option bytes, this bit will be set. And the ECCADDR records the offset address of option bytes. ECCDET bit and ECCCOR bit indicate there is a one bit error or a two bits error. This bit is cleared by writing 1. This bit is cleared by writing 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>5</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OTP_ECC</name>
              <description>If an ECC bit error is detected in OTP, this bit will be set. And the ECCADDR records the offset address of OTP. ECCDET bit and ECCCOR bit indicate there is a one bit error or a two bits error. This bit is cleared by writing 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>MF_ECC</name>
              <description>If an ECC bit error is detected in main Flash, this bit will be set. And the ECCADDR records the offset address of main Flash. ECCDET bit and ECCCOR bit indicate there is a one bit error or a two bits error. This bit is cleared by writing 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>SYS_ECC</name>
              <description>If an ECC bit error is detected in system memory, this bit will be set. And the ECCADDR records the offset address of system memory. ECCDET bit and ECCCOR bit indicate there is a one bit error or a two bits error. This bit is cleared by writing 1.</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ECCDET</name>
              <description>Two bit errors detect flag. This bit set when two bit errors is detected.</description>
              <bitOffset>1</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>ECCCOR</name>
              <description>One bit error detected and correct flag.</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
        </fields>
      </register>
      <register>
        <name>OBSTAT</name>
